  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that using scvi_n200 RNA encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion achieves high accuracy (0.725). This experiment tests whether replacing the image encoder from imagenet_vit_l (used in top performers) with resnet50 (a smaller, cheaper model) maintains performance. It clarifies the impact of image encoder choice on accuracy while keeping other key components (scvi_n200, transformer, weighted fusion) consistent. The estimated cost (≈3.0 GPU hours) is low, making it a cost-effective way to explore this uncertainty."
